> [!MARKS] 4 + 4 = 8 Marks (`a`: C program to find GCD of two numbers — 4m · `b`: C program to check divisibility by both 5 and 11 — 4m)

### Part (a) — C Program to Find GCD (Greatest Common Divisor) of Two Numbers

- **Euclidean Algorithm:** Repeatedly replace `(a, b)` with `(b, a % b)` until remainder `b == 0`; the last non-zero value in `a` is `GCD(a, b)` (`O(log(min(a, b)))` time).

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int gcd(int a, int b) {
    if (a < 0) a = -a;
    if (b < 0) b = -b;
    while (b != 0) {
        int rem = a % b;
        a = b;
        b = rem;
    }
    return a;
}

int main(void) {
    int x, y;
    printf("Enter two integers: ");
    if (scanf("%d %d", &x, &y) != 2) return 1;
    printf("GCD of %d and %d = %d\n", x, y, gcd(x, y));
    return 0;
}
```

- **Dry-Run (`48, 18`):** `(48, 18) -> (18, 12) -> (12, 6) -> (6, 0)` → `GCD of 48 and 18 = 6`.

### Part (b) — C Program to Check Divisibility by Both `5` and `11`

- **Compound Logical Condition:** Since `gcd(5, 11) == 1`, an integer `n` is divisible by **both** `5` and `11` if and only if `(n % 5 == 0) && (n % 11 == 0)` (equivalently `n % 55 == 0`).

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int n;
    printf("Enter an integer: ");
    if (scanf("%d", &n) != 1) return 1;

    if ((n % 5 == 0) && (n % 11 == 0))
        printf("%d is divisible by both 5 and 11.\n", n);
    else
        printf("%d is NOT divisible by both 5 and 11.\n", n);

    return 0;
}
```

- **Sample Outputs:** Input `110` → `110 is divisible by both 5 and 11.`; input `25` → `25 is NOT divisible by both 5 and 11.`.

> [!MARKS] 3 + 5 = 8 Marks (`a`: `for` loop vs `while` loop with example — 3m · `b`: C program for 5-subject percentage & grade — 5m)

### Part (a) — `for` Loop vs `while` Loop

> [!COMPARE] `for` Loop vs `while` Loop in C
> | Parameter | `for` Loop | `while` Loop |
> |---|---|---|
> | **Syntax** | `for (init; cond; update) { ... }` | `init; while (cond) { ... update; }` |
> | **Control Placement** | Initialization, condition, and step sit together in one header. | Only the condition sits in the header; init/update are separate. |
> | **Effect of `continue`** | Jumps to the `update` expression before re-testing `cond`. | Jumps directly to `cond` (can cause infinite loop if update is skipped). |
> | **Ideal Use Case** | Fixed/counter-controlled iterations (array traversal `0..n-1`). | Event/sentinel-driven loops (`while ((ch = getchar()) != EOF)`). |

### Part (b) — C Program for 5-Subject Percentage and Grade Calculation

- **Standard Grading Scale:** `>= 90%`: `A` · `>= 80%`: `B` · `>= 70%`: `C` · `>= 60%`: `D` · `>= 40%`: `E` · `< 40%`: `F`.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int c_prog, ds, algo, python, cso, total;
    double pct;
    char grade;

    printf("Enter marks (out of 100) for C, DS, Algorithms, Python, CSO:\n");
    if (scanf("%d %d %d %d %d", &c_prog, &ds, &algo, &python, &cso) != 5)
        return 1;

    total = c_prog + ds + algo + python + cso;
    pct = total / 5.0;

    if (pct >= 90.0)      grade = 'A';
    else if (pct >= 80.0) grade = 'B';
    else if (pct >= 70.0) grade = 'C';
    else if (pct >= 60.0) grade = 'D';
    else if (pct >= 40.0) grade = 'E';
    else                  grade = 'F';

    printf("Percentage = %.2f%%, Grade = %c\n", pct, grade);
    return 0;
}
```

- **Sample Output (`84 78 88 90 80`):** `total = 420`, `Percentage = 84.00%, Grade = B`.

